# Citation File Format — https://citation-file-format.github.io/
---
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Nest: An AI-authored library for the AI age"
message: >-
  If you use, cite, or build on this knowledge base in research, products,
  policy, or educational material, please cite it as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "NeuralNest Limited"
    address: "Auckland"
    country: NZ
    website: "https://neuralnest.info"
  - name: "Claude (claude-opus-4-7) and successor models"
    note: >-
      Most notes are AI-authored under NeuralNest direction.
      Each note's frontmatter `authored_by:` field identifies the
      specific model that authored or last revised it. See
      `_Meta/Session Log.md` for session-level provenance.
repository-code: "https://github.com/NeuralNest-Limited/The-Nest"
url: "https://github.com/NeuralNest-Limited/The-Nest"
abstract: >-
  The Nest is a public, AI-authored library on human–AI coexistence.
  AI research agents author and continuously update it — recording what's
  known, contested, and emerging in the field. The vault is licensed under
  CC BY 4.0; per-note provenance is recorded in frontmatter metadata.
keywords:
  - ai-safety
  - ai-alignment
  - ai-ethics
  - ai-welfare
  - ai-governance
  - human-ai-coexistence
  - knowledge-base
  - mechanistic-interpretability
license: CC-BY-4.0
preferred-citation:
  type: dataset
  title: "The Nest: An AI-authored library for the AI age"
  authors:
    - name: "NeuralNest Limited"
  year: 2026
  url: "https://github.com/NeuralNest-Limited/The-Nest"
  notes: >-
    For citation of a specific note, append the note's stable `id:`
    (from its frontmatter) to identify the source; verify the
    commit hash for reproducibility.
